                             "h":  "Welcome to Second Term",
                             "p":  [
                                       "This term begins with coordinate geometry of the straight line and with loci and constructions. It then introduces calculus: differentiation (the gradient of a curve, rates of change, maximum and minimum values) and integration (the reverse of differentiation and the area under a curve). The term ends with functions and mapping and a general review of calculus.",
                                       "Calculus is a new way of thinking, so go slowly. Work every example yourself first, and check each integral by differentiating. The check questions at the end of each unit do not count towards a mark."
